regressions compare published nonempty and empty saves against the
canonical in-memory encoder while retaining corruption, oversize and
concurrent publication coverage. This removes the extra payload-sized
allocation during native save publication, not the allocation required
by the caller to produce its payload.

Canonical manifest admission now compares the serializer's output directly
with the borrowed input bytes while counting every emitted byte against the
