Acceptance review, 2026-11-25: the current host and asset safety contract
is satisfied for admitted passive media and supported Linux operations.
The archive and save regressions reject traversal, links, excessive
resources and corrupt envelopes. Imports decode data without executing
original binaries. Passive overlays require explicit trusted slots,
matching media layouts and verified payloads. Bounded authenticated
network messages and owner-controlled file access constrain host effects.
Ordinary-user diagnostics demonstrate no required elevated privileges.
Future executable or gameplay-data mod support requires a new admission
and isolation review before activation; it is not presently supported.
Trusted workspace ancestry and same-user process assumptions remain.
Other native backends must demonstrate their own storage conformance
before being declared supported. This acceptance does not certify
arbitrary executable mods or protection against hostile same-user code.
